WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.602
Collection should minimize unnecessary changes while preserving enough evidence to answer the investigation questions.

00:00:06.602 --> 00:00:13.205
On a live Linux system, even listing files or running commands can create artifacts.

00:00:13.205 --> 00:00:21.937
Sometimes live collection is still necessary because volatile data, running processes, memory, or current network state may be important.

00:00:21.937 --> 00:00:25.984
The decision should be deliberate, authorized, and documented.

00:00:25.984 --> 00:00:35.994
Disk images, snapshots, targeted file collections, memory capture at a high level, log exports, and cloud records can all support an investigation.

00:00:35.994 --> 00:00:43.448
The right collection approach depends on urgency, business impact, system criticality, data sensitivity, and available tooling.

00:00:43.448 --> 00:00:47.921
Hashes help verify whether collected evidence changed after collection.

00:00:47.921 --> 00:00:55.801
Chain of custody records help document who handled evidence, when, and how it was stored or transferred.

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:59.848
Case notes are part of the evidence process.

00:00:59.848 --> 00:01:06.876
They should capture commands run, tools used, timestamps, source paths, observations, decisions, assumptions, and limitations.

00:01:06.876 --> 00:01:17.312
Notes are especially important when analysts must work from a live system or when response actions occur at the same time as collection.

00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:23.063
Later reviewers need to distinguish investigator activity from system activity under investigation.

00:01:23.063 --> 00:01:28.387
Reporting should communicate evidence, methods, findings, confidence, limitations, and supporting references.

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:37.120
A good report explains what was observed, how it was observed, what it likely means, and what remains uncertain.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:43.722
Linux forensics often involves incomplete data, rotated logs, distribution differences, and live system changes.

00:01:43.722 --> 00:01:46.491
Communicating uncertainty is not weakness.

00:01:46.491 --> 00:01:49.686
It is part of defensible investigation.
